# Oubliette: "target creature phases out until this enchantment leaves the battlefield. Tap that creature as it phases in this
# way." Bot1 enchants Bot2's Ornithopter with Rancor and then Oubliettes it: the Aura phases out with it, indirectly (CR
# 702.26g), and stays attached; Rancor does not go to a graveyard, so its own ability never returns it to hand. A creature
# phased out "until" an event does not phase in during its controller's untap step (CR 610.4a): it is still phased out in Bot2's
# turn 4. Bot2 destroys Oubliette with Disenchant, and the Ornithopter phases in at once (CR 610.4; the ruling: "immediately
# after Oubliette leaves the battlefield"), tapped, with Rancor attached (CR 702.26g: it phases in with it), a 2/2 again.

[Bot1 Deck]
